// Squads move on after taking a flag (crates/game_server/src/ai/strategy.rs): on Dalian Plant
// (64) the PLA takes the neutral Main Entrance first (-254, 153, 210), the US South Docks.
// A squad mostly at a flag its team takes (or three of it) gets its next order in the tick
// the flag changes hands ("ai flow: ... new order": the commander plans at once) and most of
// it leaves ("squad moved off": no more than a third of its members within the flag's radius
// plus 40 m, not counting the one or two left to guard it while enemies are about). Fails if
// nobody takes Main Entrance within 150 s, if no such squad gets an order elsewhere within
// 240 s after that (the first flags often fall to a tank or a few soldiers), or if it
// doesn't move off within 60 s. The server log's `ai flow:` lines say what every squad did
// after a capture (`still there 15 s after its new order: ...` lists what keeps one).
// client --scenario scenarios/ai/capture_flow.ron --out target/scenarios/ai/capture_flow
(
    level: "dalian_plant",
    size: 64,
    bots: 64,
    spectate: true,
    steps: [
        WaitReady,
        ForbidLog("panicked"),
        // Main Entrance from the south-east, 70 m off and 45 m up.
        Camera((-204.0, 198.0, 260.0), 45.0, -30.0),
        Wait(25.0),
        Screenshot("approach"),
        ExpectLog("ai flow: team 1 took Main Entrance", 150.0),
        Screenshot("taken"),
        ExpectLog("ago): new order", 240.0),
        Wait(8.0),
        Screenshot("moving_on"),
        ExpectLog("squad moved off", 60.0),
        Screenshot("moved_off"),
        // Wider, from higher up: the squads on their way to the next flags.
        Camera((-164.0, 250.0, 300.0), 45.0, -38.0),
        Wait(10.0),
        Screenshot("overview"),
        Quit,
    ],
)
